{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And He heard our voice.</b> In the blessing with which our father blessed us — that we cry out and are answered, as is said (Genesis 27:22): ״הקול קול יעקב״." "<b>And He sent an angel.</b> An actual angel, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 63): ״ומלאך פניו הושיעם״. Or it may say 'angel' about Moses, in the manner of what is said (Haggai 1:13): ״ויאמר חגי מלאך ה׳״ — for Moses was regarded in the eyes of Israel as the angel of HaShem, may He be exalted, his concern not drawn after the affairs of the body and after the chance occurrences of human beings. And a proof for this is what they said at his disappearance (Exodus 32:1): ״כי זה משה האיש אשר העלנו מארץ מצרים״ — that is, this Moses, whom we thought to be an angel, is a man, and there befell him what befalls human beings, for we did not know what had become of him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:18.401348651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}